    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by a MapStruct mapper. I followed the existing `displayName` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it's serialized in the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` and an `initials(Owner)` helper that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, each followed by a dot (e.g. `\"john\"` + `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`). It guards against null/empty names.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` now passes: creating an owner with `firstName=john`, `lastName=smith` yields `$.initials == \"J.S.\"`.",
